## Project State Summary

**Problem:** go-unix-utils re-implements GNU coreutils/moreutils utilities in Go, driven by formal specifications extracted from C source. The project stress-tests a spec-driven AI code generation pipeline (mage-claude-orchestrator) using differential testing against Homebrew GNU reference binaries.

**Architecture:** Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). `cmd/` holds per-utility Go implementations, `pkg/` provides shared libraries (testutils, sys, format), `magefiles/` wraps build orchestration. Differential testing via `pkg/testutils` compares Go and GNU binary outputs byte-for-byte.

**Current state:** 17 utilities implemented (tee, head, seq, echo, tac, nl, fold, expand, unexpand, cut, paste, uniq, comm, md5sum, sha1sum, sha256sum, sha512sum) plus foundational packages. All releases through rel05.4 are status "implemented." Code exists at generation-merged tags.

**Target release:** rel99.2 — deferred ts utility. One use case: rel99.2-uc001-ts, status "spec_complete" (PRD, use case, and test suite exist; no code on working branch).

## Priority Analysis

Release 99.2 has a single use case (ts). ts is a moreutils utility that prepends timestamps to stdin lines. It was previously generated (code at generation-merged tags from Gen A) but the current working branch has no code. The spec artifacts exist. The task is to implement `cmd/ts/main.go`. Per P2, implementation and tests are separate tasks; with a 1-task limit, implementation comes first (P8).

## Proposed Tasks

