    design_decisions:
      - id: D1
        text: "Read all flag definitions, exit codes, and edge cases from the ts PRD before implementing. The PRD is the source of truth -- do not guess behavior."
      - id: D2
        text: "Follow the same main.go structure as other cmd/ packages: sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler(), flag parsing, then core read-format-write loop."
      - id: D3
        text: "Map strftime format specifiers to Go time.Format layout strings. Build the mapping table to cover all specifiers required by the PRD. Use time.Now() for wall-clock timestamps and time.Since(start) for elapsed/incremental modes."
      - id: D4
        text: "Do NOT install packages in the build environment. Use only the Go standard library and existing pkg/ packages (pkg/sys)."

    acceptance_criteria:
      - id: AC1
        text: "cmd/ts/main.go exists, compiles cleanly with go build ./cmd/ts/, and produces a ts binary."
      - id: AC2
        text: "Running printf 'line1\\nline2\\n' | go run ./cmd/ts/ prepends a default-format timestamp to each line."
      - id: AC3
        text: "The -s flag produces elapsed timestamps (seconds since start), and -i produces incremental timestamps (seconds since last line)."
      - id: AC4
        text: "A custom strftime format string argument (e.g., '%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S') overrides the default format."
      - id: AC5
        text: "sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() is called at the start of main()."
      - id: AC6
        text: "go vet ./cmd/ts/ reports no issues."
```